## Change
The \`verify_service_tree\` test now aborts the verification even if its initial process wait times out. On cleanup it waits for the service's normal termination window, then re-enumerates uniquely marked processes and checks Linux process start time and exact arguments immediately before signaling. It no longer signals PIDs captured before an 8-second wait, which could target an unrelated process after PID reuse.

This is test-harness hardening only; production code is unchanged.

